# What never belongs in the repository.
#
# A package has no build output of its own -- `go get` compiles it in the
# consumer's build -- so most of this is what the tools and the editors leave
# behind.

# Test and coverage output.
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# What `aru view:build` writes when it compiles the views in this repository as
# a check. It mirrors a project's view tree into storage/ when it finds one, and
# writes the compiled form beside the source when it does not -- which is this
# repository, where the sources are kept at a path go mod will publish. Both are
# build output: the application compiles its own copy after publishing, so
# nothing here is ever shipped or imported, and a compiled view that reached the
# archive would be published over a page the project owns.
storage/
resources/publish/*.go
!resources/publish/*.kyse.go

# Local module resolution while something in the graph is not published.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Secrets. Nothing here reads one, and the rule stays so that the first file
# that does is not the one that finds out.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# What the editors and the operating systems leave behind.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Where the suite copies the compiled views so a compiler can see them. The go
# command skips any directory named vendor, and the build output lands under
# one, so this is the only way to put those files in front of it.
.views-compile-check/
